@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`

-- ===========================================================================
-- WHICH TAX YEARS THE DEPOSITED TEXT ANSWERS, and three gates every section of row IL-27 asks.
--
-- Like rows IL-01 to IL-08 this row answers tax years from 2024 on the consolidation retrieved on 2026-10-06, and refuses an earlier
-- tax year rather than answer it with a later text. The last amendment each section of this row shows:
-- src:1609 | סעיף 39א – זיכוי לחייל משוחרר [תיקון: תש״ס, תשס״ז, תשס״ז־6]
-- src:1619 | סעיף 39ב – זיכוי בעד שירות מילואים כלוחם [תיקון: תשפ״ו]
-- src:1648 | סעיף 40א – נקודת זיכוי לגרוש שנשא אשה אחרת [תיקון: תשל״ז, תשמ״ח־3, תשנ״ב־6]
-- src:1651 | סעיף 40ב – נקודת זיכוי לנער [תיקון: תשמ״א־8, תשנ״ב־6]
-- src:1654 | סעיף 40ג – נקודות זיכוי ליחיד שסיים לימודים לתואר אקדמי [תיקון: תשס״ה־9, תשס״ז־5, תשע״ב־4, תשע״ג־2, תשע״ו־7, תשע״ח־4]
-- src:1673 | סעיף 40ד – נקודת זיכוי ליחיד שסיים לימודי מקצוע [תיקון: תשס״ה־9, תשס״ו, תשע״ג־2, תשע״ו־6, תשע״ז־6, תשע״ח־4]
-- src:1689 | סעיף 41 – בן זוג שהיה נשוי חלק מהשנה [תיקון: תשכ״ה, תשכ״ח, תשל״ג, תשל״ד־2, תשל״ה־2, תשל״ו, תשל״ט־3, תשנ״ב־6]
-- src:1703 | סעיף 44 – זיכוי בעד הוצאות החזקת קרוב במוסד [תיקון: תשל״ה־2, תשל״ז, תשל״ח־5, תשל״ט־3, [ק״ת סכומים], תשמ״ז, תש״ן־4, תשנ״ב־6, תשנ״ה־7, תשע״ז־5, תשע״ז־11]
-- src:1707 | סעיף 45 – זיכוי בעד נטולי יכולת [תיקון: תשל״ז, תשל״ח־5, תשל״ט־3, תשמ״ח־3, תשנ״ה־7, תשס״ג־3, תשע״ז־11]
-- src:1744 | סעיף 46 – תרומה למוסד ציבורי [תיקון: תשכ״ב־2, תשכ״ח־2, תשל״ג, תשמ״ד־10, תשמ״ז, תש״ן, תשנ״ב־5, תשנ״ג־4, תשנ״ד, תשס״א־2, תשס״ה־4, תשס״ה־9, תשס״ז־3, תש״ע, תשע״ב־9, [ק״ת הודעות]]
-- src:1791 | סעיף 47א – ניכוי בשל תשלומי ביטוח לאומי ומס מקביל [תיקון: תשל״ה, תשל״ה־2, תשל״ז־3, תשמ״ד־2, תש״ן־4, תשנ״ו־3, תשנ״ז, תשפ״ג־5]
-- * ss 44 and 45 end at תשע״ז־11, s 46 at the Minister's notices, s 47A at תשפ״ג־5 (Sefer HaChukim 5783), s 39B at תשפ״ו; the others are older.
--   s 39B is the only section whose commencement is in doubt: the amending Law of 5786 is not in the source bundle, so s 39B answers
--   only the tax years 2026 and later, and refuses an earlier year (NOTES.md, "needs a source").
-- * The amounts the editorial notes print for 2024-2027 (ss 44, 45 and 46) are the consolidation's, not law: ito-il27-published-figures.l4.
-- A year after 2026 is answered on the text as it stood on 2026-10-06, a projection (assumption A2 of rows IL-01 to IL-08).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `The tax years this row answers, and three gates`

@ref the amendment lists above end with Laws that apply from tax year 2024 or are older (rows IL-02, IL-08, NOTES.md A1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first tax year row IL-27 answers` MEANS 2024

@ref the text of these sections before tax year 2024 is not verified in this row
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`row IL-27 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024` MEANS
    REFUSE "row IL-27 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"

-- Every top-level rule of the row asks this first.
GIVEN a          IS A TYPE
      `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `answer`   IS AN a
GIVETH AN a
`for tax year` `the year` `, row IL-27 answers` `answer` MEANS
    IF   `the year` AT LEAST `the first tax year row IL-27 answers`
    THEN `answer`
    ELSE `row IL-27 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024`

-- A calendar month as a single count: twelve times the year plus the month less one.
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the year`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month count of calendar month` `the month` `of` `the year` MEANS
    `the year` TIMES 12 PLUS `the month` MINUS 1

-- s 48A (src:1811) lets regulations of 5775-2014 take the Chapter's credits from a foreign worker. The regulations are deposited
-- (regulations/income-tax-credits-for-foreign-worker-regulations-5775-2014) but no row encodes them; this row reaches them and
-- declines, as rows IL-01 and IL-08 do.
@ref ITO s 48A, line 1811
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`row IL-27: section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"

@ref ITO s 48A, line 1811
GIVEN `a foreign worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the points`       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the points, unless section 48A may take them from a foreign worker:` `a foreign worker` `,` `the points` MEANS
    IF   `a foreign worker` AND `the points` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `row IL-27: section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded`
    ELSE `the points`

-- Fork F1. Sections 39A, 39B, 40A and 40B name no residence condition, where the other sections of the Chapter say "יחיד תושב ישראל".
-- RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): one named switch, default declined where residence decides; other readings kept by name.
@ref ITO ss 39A, 39B, 40A, 40B (lines 1610, 1620, 1649, 1652); compare ss 40(a), 40(b), 40C, 40D, 44, 45; fork F1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`sections 39A, 39B, 40A and 40B name no residence condition, and here residence decides` MEANS
    REFUSE "sections 39A, 39B, 40A and 40B name no residence condition, and here residence decides"

GIVETH A `A reading of the sections that name no residence condition (ss 39A, 39B, 40A, 40B)`
`the reading row IL-27 takes of the sections that name no residence condition` MEANS
    `declined where residence decides`

GIVEN `an Israeli resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the points`         IS A NUMBER
      r                    IS A `A reading of the sections that name no residence condition (ss 39A, 39B, 40A, 40B)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`points under a section that names no residence condition, for` `an Israeli resident` `, the points being` `the points` `, reading the condition as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `no residence condition` THEN `the points`
    WHEN `an Israeli resident only` THEN IF `an Israeli resident` THEN `the points` ELSE 0
    WHEN `declined where residence decides`
        THEN IF   `an Israeli resident` OR `the points` EQUALS 0
             THEN `the points`
             ELSE `sections 39A, 39B, 40A and 40B name no residence condition, and here residence decides`

-- A credit that runs over several tax years (ss 40C, 40D): the points of the runs that cover the tax year.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the runs`  IS A LIST OF `A run of credit points`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the points of the runs of credit points in tax year` `the year` `, the runs being` `the runs` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD IF   `the year` AT LEAST r's `first tax year` AND `the year` LESS THAN r's `first tax year` PLUS r's `number of tax years`
                              THEN r's `points`
                              ELSE 0)
             `the runs`)
